{"request_sha256": "3ece04db670f5ba2becb56113eb7ed98563f19745099f9ed05487da93e1b9ede", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "af67871b87f1caf764a5d748da972f77f62dc8a1876b82697f8b0be9f54772c6", "schema_sha256": "30f41622e6c7560e23f9cf8ab8aee356761b3ddea7cb1a9d1835cabc34f30ac0", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 6844}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "unknown", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["Crown fronds are far too short and thin: in render-0 and render-1 the frond length is roughly a quarter of the trunk length, against a reference (reference-0) where frond length is a large fraction of the visible trunk and the crown spread is many times the trunk diameter.", "No frond arches below the crown base in either seed; the rosette reads as a flat, near-radial starburst disc with all fronds held level to slightly upward, where the reference crown is a hemispherical/shuttlecock mass with the lowest fronds drooping well below the attachment point.", "Leaflets render as sparse, discontinuous black/green dashes strung along thin rachides rather than dense, stiff, narrow leaflets inserted in groups; the frond margin has no bristly plumose silhouette and individual fronds are not opaque at any point.", "Trunk axis is wavy in both seeds: a pronounced lateral kink with curvature reversal at roughly mid-height (render-0, render-1, clearest in render-2) rather than a straight or single gently leaning axis.", "Trunk diameter is not near-constant: it narrows markedly and continuously from the ground to the crown in render-0/render-1, with an additional local bulge at the kink in render-2.", "Trunk surface is entirely smooth in render-2 and render-3: no retained leaf-base stubs, no diamond/rhomboid spiral lattice, no fibrous matting. This is a core reference trait (trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern, trunk-fibrous-matting) reported as a mismatch against what is drawn, not invented; owner staging (fn-110 unlanded) is noted as context but does not convert the mismatch into a pass.", "No pendent fruiting bunches are present (core trait fruit-clusters-pendent); owner staging places fn-111 outside this pass, but the trait is unmatched on the evidence.", "P-BASE (render-3) is unusable as evidence: the frame is filled edge-to-edge by an out-of-focus, near-black trunk wall with no ground, no base flare and no surface detail; the manifest also marks this input visibility=hidden.", "Trunk shading is near-black and flat across all views, losing the grey-brown to reddish-brown value range and any surface texture seen in reference-0/1/2; against the fn9 spruce anchor's coherent, readable foliage and bark finish, the palm's aliased dashed leaflets and unlit trunk sit below the established catalogue finish floor."], "observations": ["Both P-WHOLE seeds (render-0, render-1) are consistent with each other in crown size, frond posture and trunk waviness; the differences between seeds are minor rotational/curvature variation, not a change in character.", "Positive findings: the stem is single and unbranched in every view, nothing grows on the trunk anywhere (no epiphytes, no foliage, no branches), and no smooth green crownshaft intervenes between crown and trunk — these match the references.", "The candidate is closer to a palm silhouette than a generic tree (radial rosette at a bare apex), but relative improvement over prior geometry is not readiness: the two first-dial traits the owner named (leaflet size, frond length) are both unmet.", "Inventory trait statements are treated as attributed interpretations; where the render offers no resolvable evidence (petiole sheath colour, basal leaflet spines, basal flare, close leaf-base pattern) the result is unknown rather than a dismissal.", "The spruce anchor (anchor-0) was used only as a finish/quality floor; no morphological weight was drawn from it."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown reads as a flat radial starburst of short, thin, dashed fronds with no frond drooping below the crown base, in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with leaflet size and frond length dials being set far below reference scale, as the owner suspects; the mechanism is not established by the images."}, {"observation": "Trunk axis carries a lateral kink with a curvature reversal near mid-height and tapers continuously from ground to crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Possibly the trunk still being driven by the shared twig taper/curve parameters (the dial table notes taper=1.0 sits outside the authored 0.05-0.6 range); not demonstrated by the renders alone."}, {"observation": "Trunk surface is smooth and featureless at both mid-trunk and close range; no leaf-base stubs, diamond lattice or fibrous matting are drawn.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with the trunk organs (fn-110) not being landed, per owner staging; recorded here as an observed mismatch, not a resolved item."}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit bunches are present on the candidate.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with fn-111 not being landed."}, {"observation": "P-BASE is filled by a defocused near-black trunk wall; the base, ground junction and leaf-base pattern are all outside or unresolvable in the frame.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Camera framing/distance for the base view appears mis-set (input is also flagged visibility=hidden); not confirmable from the image."}, {"observation": "Single unbranched stem carrying one apical rosette, with nothing growing on the trunk and no crownshaft.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Foliage colour is a dark green with pale speckling, within the green to grey-green range spanned by the references.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Trunk value is near-black and untextured across all views, below the fn9 anchor's finish floor.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "anchor-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "May be a material/lighting response issue rather than geometry; not separable from the images."}, {"observation": "No dead-frond skirt hangs below the living crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Core. Fronds are present and radiate from one apical point, but they are short, thin and held in a near-flat radial plane; none arch downward and no lower fronds droop below the crown base, so the crown does not read as the reference's rounded hemispherical/shuttlecock rosette. Defining mismatch."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Core. Leaflets appear as sparse discontinuous dashes along a bare rachis; they are too small and too widely spaced to give the plumose V-sectioned frond or the bristly margin of the references. Defining mismatch, not a finish nicety."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Core. What is drawn is a smooth cylindrical trunk with no stubs and no spiral diamond lattice at any scale. Reported as a mismatch against the reference trait; owner staging (fn-110 unlanded) explains but does not excuse it."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Core. No fibre, husk or shaggy interstitial material is drawn anywhere on the trunk."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Core, split result reported as fail on the defining clause: the stem is correctly single and unbranched, but it is neither columnar nor of roughly constant diameter — it tapers strongly from base to crown and carries a mid-height kink."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Core. No pendent bunches, stalks or fruit mass are present in either whole view. Absent rather than unassessable, so a mismatch; owner staging places fn-111 in a later pass."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary/optional refinement. No brown collar of collapsed dead fronds below the living crown; absence does not block the finish floor but is recorded as unmatched."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait, uncertain in the inventory. The candidate's dark green with pale speckling falls inside the deep-green to grey-glaucous span the references show; acceptable variation."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. The crown attachment region is only a few pixels across in every candidate view; petiole colour and sheath material cannot be assessed. Missing evidence, not a dismissal."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Inventory records this as variation spanning straight-vertical to a leaning S-curve with a smooth swollen base. The candidate's abrupt localised kink with curvature reversal lies outside that observed span, and the owner's authoritative priority explicitly excludes wavy trunks."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait, present only in reference-1/2 and absent in reference-0. The candidate trunk is bare, which is inside the reference range and matches the owner requirement that nothing grows on the trunk."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary. The candidate trunk is near-black and flat with no value range or weathering texture, against the references' grey-brown to warm reddish-brown with lighter bleached faces. Also the main gap against the fn9 anchor's finish floor."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-3", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary and uncertain in the inventory. P-BASE is unusable, and in the whole views any widening at the ground is indistinguishable from the trunk's overall taper, so no supported call is possible."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. No smooth green columnar sheath separates crown from trunk; frond bases sit directly on the stem, as in reference-1."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary and uncertain in the inventory. The proximal frond region is unresolvable in the candidate at the rendered crown scale; no assessment either way."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Variation trait, uncertain in the inventory, but the candidate falls outside it rather than within: crown spread and frond length relative to trunk length are far smaller than any reference view supports, which is the same shortfall the owner names as the first dials."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"c1474321-bc62-4dfe-b776-c5dc7ca54094","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename","ultrareview","security-review","usage-credits","extra-usage","usage","insights","recap","skill-doctor","goal","design-consent","design-revoke","list-agents","team-onboarding"],"terminal_slash_commands":["doctor","color","reload-plugins"],"apiKeySource":"none","claude_code_version":"2.1.278","output_style":"default","agents":["claude","Explore","general-purpose","Plan"],"skills":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator"],"plugins":[{"name":"flow-next","path":"/home/daniel/.claude-profiles/danithekiller93/plugins/cache/flow-next/flow-next/6.0.0","source":"flow-next@flow-next","version":"6.0.0"},{"name":"typesafe","path":"/home/daniel/.claude/plugins/cache/typesafe-ai/typesafe/0.5.7","source":"typesafe@typesafe-ai","version":"0.5.7"},{"name":"firecrawl","path":"/home/daniel/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-plugins-official/firecrawl/1.0.9","source":"firecrawl@claude-plugins-official","version":"1.0.9"},{"name":"rust-analyzer-lsp","path":"/home/daniel/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-plugins-official/rust-analyzer-lsp/1.0.0","source":"rust-analyzer-lsp@claude-plugins-official","version":"1.0.0"}],"capabilities":["interrupt_receipt_v1","interrupt_cancel_queued_v1","msg_lifecycle_v1"],"analytics_disabled":false,"product_feedback_disabled":false,"uuid":"e7b0dc28-fe03-4163-bbde-d58555086d70","messaging_socket_path":"/run/user/1000/cc-socks/1650185.sock","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required"}
